51
00:02:09,190 --> 00:02:13,570
EPISODE 36:
EACH ONE'S RESOLUTION

52
00:02:09,810 --> 00:02:11,990
The match continues!

53
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:15,780
Alright. Everyone forward.

54
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:16,780
Yes!

55
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:21,810
Although Azumaichi has been completely focused on defense until now, all their players are now pushing forward.

56
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:23,030
Come at us if you dare!

57
00:02:23,030 --> 00:02:26,290
Both teams are battling in midfield!

58
00:02:26,290 --> 00:02:30,500
Soda is personally marking Tsubasa!

59
00:02:34,550 --> 00:02:36,670
Azumaichi is attacking with ambition!

60
00:02:36,670 --> 00:02:38,490
However, Nankatsu is resisting!

61
00:02:38,490 --> 00:02:41,340
The excitement is at its peak!

62
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:42,970
Don't lose, Nankatsu!

63
00:02:42,970 --> 00:02:44,930
Come on, Azumaichi!

64
00:02:47,430 --> 00:02:49,390
Nankatsu steals the ball!

65
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:51,660
Alright, Tsubasa is free....

66
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:55,600
Come on, Iwami!

67
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:56,150
Okay!

68
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:59,220
Nankatsu passes the ball to Izawa.

69
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:01,710
Can Izawa control the attack in Tsubasa's place?

70
00:03:01,710 --> 00:03:02,950
Come on, Taki!

71
00:03:02,950 --> 00:03:05,660
Izawa passes the ball to Taki.

72
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:06,790
I won't allow it!

73
00:03:06,790 --> 00:03:07,500
What?!

74
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:09,370
My turn!

75
00:03:09,370 --> 00:03:10,620
Guys, fall back!

76
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:12,420
Azumaichi's attacks are coming one after another!

77
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:15,960
But Kisugi intercepted the pass!

78
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:16,920
Tsubasa!

79
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:20,680
Soda is still tightly marking Tsubasa!

80
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:27,100
Neither team could find an opening to create a position.

81
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:29,180
Only 5 minutes left!

82
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:32,520
Take it!

83
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:34,630
Ishizaki clears the ball.

84
00:03:34,630 --> 00:03:37,360
Azumaichi's attack is thwarted once again.

85
00:03:38,110 --> 00:03:40,570
The match is starting now! Let's go!

86
00:03:40,570 --> 00:03:42,110
No way!

87
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:46,780
Soda stops marking Tsubasa and starts running towards the loose ball.

88
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,970
Soda is approaching the ball!

89
00:03:48,970 --> 00:03:51,540
On the other side, Nankatsu's Taki challenges him.

90
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:53,650
Taki, I'm counting on you.

91
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:54,170
Alright!

92
00:03:54,170 --> 00:03:55,210
Take this!

93
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:57,880
Razor Tackle!

94
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:03,300
Soda steals the ball and leads the attack himself!

95
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:06,140
Azumaichi looks like they will find the goal this time.

96
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:07,760
Morisaki, he's going to shoot!

97
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:10,270
Watch out for the ball's curve.

98
00:04:10,270 --> 00:04:10,850
Understood!

99
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:14,690
Tsubasa...

100
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:18,070
Your Dead Leaf shot is still not good enough.

101
00:04:18,770 --> 00:04:23,150
But my Razor Shot is 100% mastered!

102
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:29,660
And the Razor shot works in any situation!

103
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:32,660
We've got the match!

104
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:36,560
Morisaki, the other side!

105
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:38,540
Jump to the other side this time!

106
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:45,220
Soda performs the Razor Shot!

107
00:04:45,950 --> 00:04:48,190
The ball curves differently this time!

108
00:04:48,190 --> 00:04:49,850
It's heading to the left!

109
00:04:49,850 --> 00:04:52,060
This is the Reverse Razor Shot!

110
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:55,840
He sa-saved it!

111
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:58,140
Morisaki saved it this time!

112
00:04:58,140 --> 00:04:59,480
An incredible save!

113
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:01,420
Morisaki!

114
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:03,150
You did it! Nice save!

115
00:05:03,810 --> 00:05:05,660
Alright! Come on, Morisaki!

116
00:05:07,410 --> 00:05:08,620
Okay! Tsubasa!

117
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:12,790
Since Soda went forward to attack, Tsubasa is completely free!

118
00:05:12,790 --> 00:05:13,540
Alright!

119
00:05:13,540 --> 00:05:17,710
Since Azumaichi attacked with all their players, no one is left on defense!

120
00:05:17,710 --> 00:05:19,170
Damn it! Go back!

121
00:05:19,170 --> 00:05:21,090
Come on, Tsubasa!

122
00:05:21,090 --> 00:05:23,950
Tsubasa is unmarked for the first time in this match.

123
00:05:23,950 --> 00:05:26,240
He can move freely for the first time!

124
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:28,180
Tsubasa, your leg...

125
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:29,610
I'm free!

126
00:05:29,610 --> 00:05:33,770
If I don't score this goal, I can only dream of the 3rd championship.

127
00:05:35,390 --> 00:05:39,270
Tsubasa passes the last defender and advances towards the goal!

128
00:05:39,270 --> 00:05:41,960
It's no use. No one can stop him now!

129
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:46,810
Goal!

130
00:05:46,810 --> 00:05:49,000
Tsubasa's first goal of the tournament!

131
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,120
And the victory goal!

132
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:51,810
There!

133
00:05:51,810 --> 00:05:52,540
I did it!

134
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:54,310
Nankatsu takes the lead!

135
00:05:54,310 --> 00:06:02,300
Minutes before the end of the match, Captain Tsubasa scored the goal that would lead his team to victory!

136
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:03,860
You did it, Tsubasa!

137
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:05,840
We're ahead!

138
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:07,920
You worried us for nothing!

139
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:10,050
You did it, Tsubasa!

140
00:06:10,050 --> 00:06:12,560
Everything worked out with this goal.

141
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:15,320
How did he know?!

142
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:17,980
I've never used my Reverse Razor Shot in any match until now...

143
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:21,270
Not even once...

144
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:27,530
The final whistle blows!

145
00:06:27,530 --> 00:06:32,280
Azumaichi fought until the very end, but unfortunately for them, time ran out.

146
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:34,280
Score is 2-1.

147
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:39,590
The reigning champion Nankatsu MS, though they struggled in this match, still ends it with a victory.

148
00:06:39,590 --> 00:06:43,290
Ohhh..! We barely won this match.

149
00:06:43,290 --> 00:06:45,960
Azumaichi couldn't get the result for their efforts.

150
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:48,550
But they put up a good fight against Nankatsu.

151
00:06:49,170 --> 00:06:50,740
Well done, guys.

152
00:06:50,740 --> 00:06:52,050
You did great!

153
00:06:52,630 --> 00:06:55,680
You did a good job as Osaka's representative, Soda.

154
00:06:55,680 --> 00:07:00,770
Tsubasa Ozora... You must not be left unmarked.

155
00:07:00,770 --> 00:07:02,330
You're right.

156
00:07:02,330 --> 00:07:06,570
If Soda had continued marking Tsubasa instead of trying to push forward,

157
00:07:06,570 --> 00:07:09,030
the match would have ended in a draw.

158
00:07:09,030 --> 00:07:12,660
It seems we will be the ones to beat Nankatsu.

159
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:13,530
Yes.

160
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:17,710
Tsubasa.

161
00:07:18,290 --> 00:07:19,790
Soda...

162
00:07:19,790 --> 00:07:23,750
How did you predict my Reverse Razor Shot?

163
00:07:23,750 --> 00:07:28,550
Good question. If Tsubasa hadn't told me, I likely wouldn't have saved it.

164
00:07:28,550 --> 00:07:31,380
Let's call it a sixth sense.

165
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:36,430
When I looked at the angle between your legs, I just knew you'd shoot that way.

166
00:07:36,430 --> 00:07:37,890
"Just knew," huh...

167
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:42,520
You see, I'm having a hard time putting spin on the ball.

168
00:07:43,890 --> 00:07:45,490
I can see that.

169
00:07:45,490 --> 00:07:51,230
I guess I won't be able to master the dead leaf shot like you.

170
00:07:51,230 --> 00:07:53,090
I'm sure you can do it.

171
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:57,370
By the way, is your leg okay?

172
00:07:57,370 --> 00:07:59,660
Your leg? Did something happen to your leg, Tsubasa?

173
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:03,200
Tsubasa injured his leg a little.

174
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:05,180
WHAT?!

175
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:09,700
It was already hurting from time to time.

176
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:10,760
Alright then.

177
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:16,840
You devastated us. Don't come back without the championship.

178
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,640
No problem on that front.

179
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:22,480
Alright then... See you, Tsubasa.

180
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:25,400
Damn it! We lost!

181
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,360
Don't be sad and cry, guys.

182
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,970
Go home with your heads held high!

183
00:08:28,970 --> 00:08:30,230
Soda...

184
00:08:30,230 --> 00:08:32,230
Makoto Soda...

185
00:08:32,230 --> 00:08:36,490
I thought you were a bit of a punk, but you're a good guy.

186
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:43,500
Nankatsu won, albeit with difficulty.

187
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:44,610
You're right.

188
00:08:44,610 --> 00:08:49,710
Can we consider Soda as a rival for Tsubasa?

189
00:08:50,330 --> 00:08:51,960
Maybe.

190
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:55,340
About that shot Tsubasa took...

191
00:08:56,400 --> 00:09:00,060
Did he do it on purpose? Or was it just...

192
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:02,980
Of course he did it on purpose.

193
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:06,940
The dead leaf shot is the shot Tsubasa is trying to master.

194
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:08,730
Dead leaf shot?

195
00:09:08,730 --> 00:09:20,560
Yes. If Tsubasa masters this shot, we could bring him into the Japanese national team right now.

196
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:25,790
There's no doubt about it.

197
00:09:25,790 --> 00:09:30,960
I hear the dead leaf shot is a move seen in South America, especially in Brazil.

198
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:33,710
It's a very difficult move even for professionals.

199
00:09:33,710 --> 00:09:37,090
Mastering this move in the 3rd year of middle school...

200
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:42,350
Tsubasa Ozora is truly an opponent to be feared.

201
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:45,850
We've passed the 5-minute mark of the second half.

202
00:09:45,850 --> 00:09:49,100
The second match of the Traditional Middle School Football Tournament

203
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:51,650
FIGHT! FIGHT! Toho!

204
00:09:49,770 --> 00:09:54,690
is between Toho Academy from Tokyo and Matsukami MS from Nara.

205
00:09:51,650 --> 00:09:54,690
GO! GO! Matsukami! CRUSH THEM!

206
00:09:54,690 --> 00:09:57,700
Even though it's the second half, we still haven't seen a goal.

207
00:09:57,700 --> 00:10:03,200
Toho Academy is a team considered as one of Nankatsu's rivals.

208
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:08,290
Despite their dominance, they still lack a strong enough attack to score a goal.

209
00:10:08,290 --> 00:10:10,690
The absence of their ace player is felt.

210
00:10:10,690 --> 00:10:15,970
Kojiro Hyuga is sitting on the bench, just watching.

211
00:10:16,650 --> 00:10:17,670
Is he injured?

212
00:10:17,670 --> 00:10:22,220
Or is he being kept on the sidelines to let young players gain experience?

213
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:25,500
Unexpected things are happening at the tournament.

214
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:28,210
But we still don't know the details.

215
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:29,480
Brother...

216
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:32,020
Kojiro isn't playing.

217
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:35,780
For now, Kojiro is observing from the bench.

218
00:10:35,780 --> 00:10:40,240
Their opponents, Matsukami MS, known for their defense, have been doing quite well so far.

219
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:43,370
They're not giving Toho any space.

220
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:46,870
They stole the ball!

221
00:10:46,870 --> 00:10:49,800
With Hyuga not playing, it's impossible for us to lose to Toho.

222
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:52,380
We'll score the goal and Hyuga will take the field!

223
00:10:52,380 --> 00:10:54,750
This time Matsukami is counter-attacking!

224
00:10:54,750 --> 00:10:56,090
Go!

225
00:10:56,090 --> 00:10:56,840
Alright!

226
00:10:56,840 --> 00:11:00,340
Goalkeeper Wakashimazu catches the ball firmly!

227
00:11:00,810 --> 00:11:02,990
He isn't the number one middle school goalkeeper for nothing.

228
00:11:02,990 --> 00:11:05,070
He doesn't let goals in that easily.

229
00:11:05,070 --> 00:11:06,350
Hey, Takeshi!

230
00:11:08,730 --> 00:11:11,310
It's Toho's turn to counter-attack!

231
00:11:11,310 --> 00:11:12,310
Sorimachi!

232
00:11:12,310 --> 00:11:13,110
There's a gap!

233
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:17,510
He did it!

234
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:21,730
A perfect shot from Sorimachi, playing in Hyuga's place.

235
00:11:21,730 --> 00:11:26,490
Sawada made an incredible through pass. It was the kind that goes into the curriculum.

236
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:31,150
Even though Hyuga isn't playing, Toho is still quite strong.

237
00:11:31,150 --> 00:11:32,050
What should I write?

238
00:11:32,050 --> 00:11:33,750
That they're saving Hyuga for later?

239
00:11:33,750 --> 00:11:35,590
Or is it an injury story?

240
00:11:35,590 --> 00:11:41,210
Coach Kitazume hasn't made any comments since saying he won't let Hyuga play.

241
00:11:41,210 --> 00:11:45,970
There's nothing we can do. Maybe we should put Sorimachi, Sawada, and Wakashimazu in the headline.

242
00:11:47,850 --> 00:11:53,120
The coach says he won't let Hyuga play, but we can't become champions without him.

243
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:55,900
Especially we can't beat Nankatsu.

244
00:11:56,870 --> 00:11:58,150
Let's just hold on until the finals for now.

245
00:11:58,690 --> 00:12:03,660
Until then, we must keep winning with our own strength without our captain.

246
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:20,590
Toho Academy attacks again!

247
00:12:20,590 --> 00:12:21,450
Let's score another goal!

248
00:12:21,450 --> 00:12:22,340
Yes!

249
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:24,590
An incredible cross from Sawada.

250
00:12:24,590 --> 00:12:27,600
Sorimachi controlled the ball with his chest and...

251
00:12:28,750 --> 00:12:29,720
He shoots!

252
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:33,640
W-What?!

253
00:12:48,660 --> 00:12:50,160
Goal!

254
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:52,830
Toho Academy easily scores the second goal.

255
00:12:52,830 --> 00:12:54,160
Score is 2-0.

256
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:57,170
Hey, did you catch that?

257
00:12:57,170 --> 00:12:59,840
Of course! Sorimachi's second goal, right?

258
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:01,300
Idiot, not that!

259
00:13:01,300 --> 00:13:03,300
I'm talking about Hyuga's shot!

260
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:03,590
What?

261
00:13:13,980 --> 00:13:16,440
I'm going back to the clubhouse.

262
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:20,010
Hyuga...

263
00:13:21,150 --> 00:13:26,150
~Anime Severler~
Instagram: AnimeSeverlerrr

264
00:13:28,030 --> 00:13:32,540
— SAITAMA WORLD STADIUM —

265
00:13:29,410 --> 00:13:32,540
The second day of the Traditional Middle School Football Tournament.

266
00:13:32,540 --> 00:13:36,540
— BAY COAST STADIUM —

267
00:13:33,110 --> 00:13:38,220
People have already started filling the stadiums.

268
00:13:41,630 --> 00:13:45,470
They said Hyuga had disappeared, but now he's just watching the match from the bench.

269
00:13:45,470 --> 00:13:48,780
There are rumors that he's injured.

270
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:51,410
Nankatsu had quite a hard time yesterday, didn't they?

271
00:13:51,410 --> 00:13:54,850
I heard that Soda from Azumaichi MS did a good job.

272
00:13:54,850 --> 00:13:56,190
Now pull the shot!

273
00:13:57,480 --> 00:14:00,090
Is Tsubasa's leg okay?

274
00:14:00,090 --> 00:14:03,820
I hope he recovers after resting today.

275
00:14:03,820 --> 00:14:04,640
Hopefully.

276
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:06,900
All we can do is pray.

277
00:14:07,850 --> 00:14:10,490
How did Tsubasa manage to hide the condition of his leg

278
00:14:10,490 --> 00:14:14,160
from us.

279
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:16,030
I ask myself the same question.

280
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:21,980
Tsubasa was being considerate; he didn't want us to worry in the middle of the match.

281
00:14:21,980 --> 00:14:23,750
I know that much, but...

282
00:14:23,750 --> 00:14:28,630
But now that we know we shouldn't overwork him, we realize we have to work even harder.

283
00:14:28,630 --> 00:14:32,020
It's our turn to work hard.

284
00:14:32,020 --> 00:14:33,940
Yes, you're right.

285
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:34,640
Alright!

286
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:39,670
Let's lead Nankatsu to the championship with our own strength!

287
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:40,650
Yes!

288
00:14:41,730 --> 00:14:45,690
Tsubasa's injury has greatly motivated the team.

289
00:14:46,790 --> 00:14:48,290
Yes, it's quite good.

290
00:14:48,290 --> 00:14:50,450
There's no problem with the bone.

291
00:14:50,450 --> 00:14:53,020
How is your leg now?

292
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:56,700
After a day's rest, there's not much pain left.

293
00:14:56,700 --> 00:14:59,620
It's just a minor sprain.

294
00:14:59,620 --> 00:15:03,570
But as you said, your leg seems prone to these kinds of injuries.

295
00:15:03,570 --> 00:15:05,160
So you have to be careful.

296
00:15:05,160 --> 00:15:05,960
Of course.

297
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:09,970
You need to bandage your foot for your next match.

298
00:15:09,970 --> 00:15:14,520
Don't push yourself too hard today and take a break from training.

299
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:15,720
Understood.

300
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:17,920
Take care.

301
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:20,350
Thank you very much, sir.

302
00:15:20,350 --> 00:15:21,980
Thank you very much.

303
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:27,480
Even though I come here often, I really don't like hospitals.

304
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:30,250
It's good that there's nothing serious with your leg.

305
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:31,780
It's a relief.

306
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:32,660
Exactly.

307
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:38,510
At a time like this, not being able to play in a match as a captain would be a disaster.

308
00:15:38,510 --> 00:15:41,120
You've worked hard for this.

309
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:44,630
Thanks to our manager.

310
00:15:44,630 --> 00:15:47,880
Even you don't believe what you're saying.

311
00:15:53,250 --> 00:15:54,640
What a big park this is.

312
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:58,270
It's quite crowded since it's Sunday.

313
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:21,800
Oh, right! If I can't train today, I should go and

314
00:16:21,800 --> 00:16:25,790
watch the match between Nishikigaoka MS and Ozusan MS.

315
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:28,450
Manabu already went to observe.

316
00:16:28,450 --> 00:16:31,510
If we hurry, we can make it before Furano's match.

317
00:16:31,510 --> 00:16:33,260
Of course.

318
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:34,530
Alright, let's go!

319
00:16:34,530 --> 00:16:35,110
Wait-

320
00:16:35,110 --> 00:16:35,760
Tsubasa!

321
00:16:36,670 --> 00:16:40,520
Oh my god, he's running with an injured foot.

322
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:47,770
Where's the captain?

323
00:16:47,770 --> 00:16:49,230
He's not on the field.

324
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:54,570
Coach, Hyuga still hasn't come.

325
00:16:54,570 --> 00:16:56,140
Hyuga won't be coming.

326
00:16:57,350 --> 00:16:59,950
This is the last tournament for the 3rd years.

327
00:16:59,950 --> 00:17:04,410
Since Hyuga won't be playing in this tournament, he doesn't need to practice here.

328
00:17:04,410 --> 00:17:06,380
That's why I told him not to come.

329
00:17:06,380 --> 00:17:08,860
No way!

330
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:12,440
Coach, we can't be champions without Hyuga!

331
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:13,880
The coach is right.

332
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:14,760
Shut your mouths!

333
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:16,720
Are you defying me?!

334
00:17:18,510 --> 00:17:21,600
You must follow my orders!

335
00:17:21,600 --> 00:17:25,620
Wakashimazu, from now on, you are the team captain until the tournament is over.

336
00:17:26,140 --> 00:17:27,120
Understood?

337
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:30,450
C-Coach...

338
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:34,960
Hyuga...

339
00:17:39,620 --> 00:17:43,730
He's surrounded by three players but still won't give up the ball!

340
00:17:43,730 --> 00:17:45,540
Incredible...

341
00:17:44,320 --> 00:17:45,540
I'm back!

342
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:48,300
Brother!

343
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:50,540
I hope you're all well!

344
00:17:51,020 --> 00:17:52,920
Kojiro!

345
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:01,810
Matsuyama is holding the ball!

346
00:18:01,810 --> 00:18:02,470
Right here!

347
00:18:04,470 --> 00:18:07,730
Matsuyama distracts his opponents and passes!

348
00:18:08,540 --> 00:18:08,980
It's yours!

349
00:18:10,250 --> 00:18:11,020
Nice!

350
00:18:11,020 --> 00:18:13,500
Furano continues their passing traffic.

351
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:14,860
Incredible teamwork!

352
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:20,380
Furano's players are showing very disciplined team play this year.

353
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:23,950
It's also worth mentioning that they are playing a very gentlemanly game!

354
00:18:24,610 --> 00:18:25,450
Captain!

355
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:33,360
Yes!

356
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:36,510
Their captain Matsuyama completed the attack with a goal.

357
00:18:36,510 --> 00:18:38,510
Score is 6-0.

358
00:18:38,510 --> 00:18:39,810
They did it.

359
00:18:39,810 --> 00:18:43,510
It was worth coming all the way from Hokkaido.

360
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:47,820
And the match is over.

361
00:18:47,820 --> 00:18:49,370
Score is 6-0.

362
00:18:49,370 --> 00:18:56,530
Hokkaido's representative Furano MS defeated Okayama's representative Sakucho MS with wonderful team play!

363
00:18:56,530 --> 00:18:59,150
Furano advances to the 2nd round.

364
00:18:59,150 --> 00:19:06,080
We consider Furano to be a championship contender like Nankatsu and Toho.

365
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:10,700
Alright, guys, let's keep this up and take the championship flag to Hokkaido.

366
00:19:10,700 --> 00:19:11,540
Yes!

367
00:19:12,410 --> 00:19:23,990
The next match between Nishikigaoka MS from Kanagawa and Ozusan MS from Kochi will be at 11:30.

368
00:19:23,990 --> 00:19:27,760
Oh, it seems we arrived just in time for Furano's match.

369
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:33,560
After all that running, is your leg okay, Tsubasa?

370
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:35,560
Oh, I forgot about it!

371
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:37,190
Oh, you...!

372
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,200
There he is!

373
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:40,160
Manabu!

374
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:40,820
Huh?

375
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:42,690
Oh, Tsubasa!

376
00:19:42,690 --> 00:19:44,280
How's your leg?

377
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:46,120
Quite well.

378
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:47,680
Nothing serious.

379
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,830
Really?

380
00:19:48,830 --> 00:19:51,090
How was Furano?

381
00:19:51,090 --> 00:19:53,090
Oh yes, they're quite good.

382
00:19:53,090 --> 00:19:56,240
They've improved a lot compared to last year.

383
00:19:56,240 --> 00:19:59,200
They'll be a big obstacle ahead of us.

384
00:19:59,200 --> 00:19:59,840
Is that so?

385
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:05,780
Nishikigaoka and Ozusan are not opponents we can beat easily.

386
00:20:05,780 --> 00:20:09,350
It seems they won't let us win the Traditional Tournament so easily.

387
00:20:10,330 --> 00:20:12,350
Whoever comes, I will not lose.

388
00:20:12,350 --> 00:20:16,110
I will go to Brazil undefeated like this.

389
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:19,360
Tsubasa, what are you doing here?

390
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:22,500
The doctor gave you a chance to take some time for yourself.

391
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:25,650
You two need to spend more time together.

392
00:20:27,110 --> 00:20:29,910
Ah! Tsubasa is over there!

393
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:32,300
You guys came too?

394
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:33,080
Yes.

395
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:35,080
The morning practice is over.

396
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:36,790
We came to watch the match too.

397
00:20:36,790 --> 00:20:39,050
How was it, Tsubasa?

398
00:20:39,050 --> 00:20:42,090
Quite well.

399
00:20:42,090 --> 00:20:44,420
We're not talking about your leg...

400
00:20:44,420 --> 00:20:45,940
You two were alone, right?

401
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:47,720
At least you held hands, didn't you?

402
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:49,220
With the manager, I mean.

403
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:51,500
How was it?

404
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:53,440
How did it go for you, Tsubasa?

405
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:55,150
Nothing happened.

406
00:20:56,230 --> 00:20:59,450
What are you ladies talking about?

407
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:04,490
They're all so curious.

408
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:09,240
Huh?

409
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:11,500
Are you leaving Toho Academy?

410
00:21:11,500 --> 00:21:14,330
We had a small disagreement with the coach.

411
00:21:14,330 --> 00:21:17,250
It seems my school scholarship will be canceled.

412
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:24,560
If it's canceled, and considering Toho is a private school,

413
00:21:24,560 --> 00:21:28,640
for poor people like us, there's no choice but to leave.

414
00:21:29,320 --> 00:21:31,010
That's not fair, brother!

415
00:21:31,010 --> 00:21:32,780
No problem.

416
00:21:32,780 --> 00:21:37,520
I'll go back to middle school and graduate while working part-time.

417
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:41,780
But Kojiro, if you do that, you won't be able to focus on the football you love.

418
00:21:41,780 --> 00:21:43,780
There's nothing to be done.

419
00:21:43,780 --> 00:21:46,680
My school football life ends with middle school.

420
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:54,090
I won't be able to dedicate as much time to football as I have until now,

421
00:21:54,090 --> 00:21:55,960
but I can keep playing on my own.

422
00:21:56,390 --> 00:21:58,820
I'll keep playing while working.

423
00:21:58,820 --> 00:22:00,460
Kojiro.

424
00:22:00,460 --> 00:22:03,940
If you're forcing me to leave, it's fine.

425
00:22:03,940 --> 00:22:05,420
But in return...

426
00:22:09,980 --> 00:22:17,620
But in return, I will face Tsubasa and defeat him with this right leg.

427
